re plus an -ing form for an activity in progress now. The form of be agrees with the subject.","examples":["The dog is sleeping by the fire.","We are discussing the route."]},{"title":"Building the verb","explanation":"Many verbs add -ing. Usually remove a final silent e; some short verbs double their last consonant. Learn spelling with the verb.","examples":["write → writing","cut → cutting"]},{"title":"Questions and negatives","explanation":"Move be before the subject in a question. Put not after be in a negative. Keep the -ing form in both.","examples":["Are they loading the van?","I am not using the lift."]}],"tips":["Read the full context before choosing.","Check the explanation, including after a correct answer.","A passing practice session is useful feedback, not a language certificate."],"source":"seed","provenance":{"version":"foundations-2026-09-v1","authorship":"Grammacho; generated offline with AI assistance","kind":"original-guidance-aligned","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending","referenceIds":["bc-continuous","pcc-esol"],"assessment":"Practice only; levels are approximate teaching labels, not validated CEFR assessment."}}'::jsonb j) payload
